From 11535fe7b6ef2d92d9cfceb26dbbf22f7e000509 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:31:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 150/152] drm/panfrost: Unmask the MMU interrupts at init

panfrost_jm_init() enables the job interrupts, but the MMU interrupts are
only unmasked by panfrost_mmu_reset(), which first runs from
panfrost_device_reset() on runtime resume. Without CONFIG_PM there is no
runtime resume, so MMU_INT_MASK stays 0 after probe: the first GPU page
fault, the tiler heap growing for the first frame, is never serviced and
the job hangs until the scheduler timeout resets the GPU (which unmasks
the interrupts, so everything works afterwards).

Seen on the Exynos9810 (CONFIG_PM=n): "gpu sched timeout, js=1,
status=0x8" on the first job of every boot (GDM's first frame) and of
every module load, panfrost-mmu interrupt count 0. With the interrupts
unmasked at init the first job completes and the heap faults are
handled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
index 4a3162c3b..2414e2811 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -970,6 +970,16 @@ int panfrost_mmu_init(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Unmask the MMU interrupts here, as panfrost_jm_init() does for the
+	 * job interrupts. Otherwise only panfrost_mmu_reset() unmasks them,
+	 * which first runs on runtime resume: without CONFIG_PM there is
+	 * none, so the first page fault (tiler heap growth) went unhandled
+	 * and the job hung until the scheduler timeout reset the GPU.
+	 */
+	mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_CLEAR, ~0);
+	mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_MASK, ~0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
